  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Trinidadian stick-fighting song, in which a chantwell leads call-and-response chants while drummers play skin drums for paired fighters in the ring (gayelle). Kalinda was central to the 19th-century canboulay and street carnival and is named among the roots of calypso; Alan Lomax recorded kalinda chants in Trinidad in 1962. The membrane-drum card stands in for the goatskin drums.",
